  "notes": "USAGE:\n{補修|ほしゅう} refers to repairing things that have deteriorated over time, particularly structures and infrastructure. It implies restoring something to a functional state rather than replacing it entirely.\n\nCOMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- {補修|ほしゅう}{工事|こうじ} (repair work/construction)\n- {補修|ほしゅう}{費用|ひよう} (repair costs)\n- {道路|どうろ}の{補修|ほしゅう} (road repair)\n- {補修|ほしゅう}する (to repair)\n\nSIMILAR WORDS:\n{修理|しゅうり} is a broader term for fixing broken items (appliances, machines). {補修|ほしゅう} focuses on maintaining or patching up structures and facilities. {修繕|しゅうぜん} is more formal and often used for building maintenance.",
